Clause G8.8.2 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): Stormwater Drainage System must be designed to comply with Part E of this Development Control Plan.

Clause G8.8.2 - environmental_protection (environmental_protection): Any development of the site must also consider the following matters: a. ‘water’: reduction in potable water use, water reuse and use of other water sources; b. ‘land use and ecology’: reduction in the impact on the ecosystem.

Clause G8.9.1 - parking (development_control): Two (2) vehicular access/egress points are to be located as per Figure G44 except if 141 and 159 Allen Street are amalgamated and developed at the same time in which case one (Access/Egress 1) vehicle ingress/egress point immediately north of Building A will be acceptable.

Clause G8.9.1 - setback (development_control): Ramps and excavation required for vehicle access and egress is to be setback a minimum of $4 . 5 \mathsf { m }$ from the property boundary to allow for urban design outcomes in the streetscape.

Clause G8.9.1 - other (development_control): Vehicular access and egress is to be no less than 6m in width.

Clause G8.9.2 - parking (development_control): The total number of car spaces for residents and visitors shall equate to the minimum of: 
a. 0.6 spaces per 1-bedroom dwelling;   
b. 0.9 spaces per 2-bedroom dwelling;   
c. 1.1 spaces per 3-bedroom dwelling or any dwelling with a greater number of bedrooms.

Clause G8.9.2 - parking (development_control): All bicycle parking is to comply with the provisions contained in the ‘Parking’ section of this Plan.
